From 58396e9d7c3e4d3350b5c4d624d284a56926f0d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Myghi63 <myghi63@disroot.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:40:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy.recovery: allow permissive recovery and su on user
 builds

Flasher zips (microG installer, gapps, AnyKernel kernel zips) run their
update-binaries in the recovery domain. LOS makes recovery permissive only
on userdebug/eng; the user variant refuses permissive domains
(build/soong/policy.go). Whitelist recovery (mirroring that userdebug
behavior) and su: AnyKernel3 sets its process context to u:r:su:s0 to
loop-mount apex payloads, and on a user build the su domain is otherwise
restricted enough that the setcon kills the installer mid-install.
microdroid uses the same module property for its su domain.

Change-Id: Ia9972163218c726ffd681152d551950fe6db249b
---
 Android.bp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index e10d906b0..beaa31d1c 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -757,6 +757,7 @@ se_policy_binary {
     ],
     stem: "sepolicy",
     recovery: true,
+    permissive_domains_on_user_builds: ["recovery", "su"],
 }
 
 //////////////////////////////////
